# Codex Maintenance Rule

RULE: Update unified-trading-codex in the same PR as any architectural code change. Code change without codex update = incomplete task.
WHY: Codex is the single source of truth for all patterns — stale docs cause divergence across 30+ repos.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/contribution-guide.md

## When to Update

- New architectural pattern or design decision
- New standard established (e.g. versioning, event counts)
- Deviation from existing pattern (document WHY)
- Cross-service infrastructure refactor

## Where to Update

Prefer updating existing files:
- `02-data/` — data patterns, subscription models
- `03-observability/` — event logging, monitoring
- `04-architecture/` — service architecture, communication
- `06-coding-standards/` — code organization, quality gates

Only create new files when topic has no existing home or requires >500 lines.

## Codex vs PM Boundary

Not sure if something belongs in codex or PM? Consult the decision tree:
CODEX: `13-codex-governance/SSOT-BOUNDARY.md`

Short rule: codex = "what must be true", PM = "what is happening right now". No absolute machine-specific paths in either repo; always use workspace-relative paths.

## DRY Principle

Reference existing patterns rather than duplicating. Link to the section; don't repeat the content. Per-service docs document deviations only — not the universal pattern.

## Implementation-Alignment Rule

Code change + codex update must be in the same PR. Commit message MUST reference which codex section was updated (e.g. `docs(codex): update 06-coding-standards/configuration.md`).
